        "  freeze: true\n",
        "  python: \"C:/GitHub/Computer_Vision_Assessment/venv/Scripts/python.exe\"\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "# ✈️ Computer Vision QA Assessment for Airport Apron Annotation Pipelines\n",
        "\n",
        "## 📘 Introduction\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook provides a robust framework for performing **quality assurance (QA)** on annotated image datasets used in **computer vision (CV) pipelines** for airport apron operations. These operations involve detecting and tracking aircraft, vehicles, ground crew, and equipment to ensure timely and safe turnaround processes. Reliable annotation is critical in such safety-critical environments, where every mislabeled object or faulty bounding box can undermine model accuracy and operational trust.\n",
        "\n",
        "We focus on a synthetic dataset representing apron scenarios, using per-frame CSV annotations. The QA framework evaluates the correctness of bounding boxes, label consistency, and visual alignment before converting the data into the **COCO** format—a widely used standard for training object detection models.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 🧠 Techniques Used\n",
        "\n",
        "- **CSV Parsing (via `pandas`)**: Structured loading of annotation files\n",
        "- **Bounding Box QA Checks**: Ensure spatial validity and logical coherence\n",
        "- **Visual Validation**: Overlay annotations on images for human-in-the-loop inspection\n",
        "- **COCO Format Conversion**: Interoperable export for ML pipelines\n",
        "- **Schema Revalidation**: Final consistency checks after format transformation\n",
        "\n",
        "## 🗂 Dataset Description\n",
        "\n",
        "The dataset includes synthetic images of airport apron scenes and CSV annotation files with the following structure:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `frame_id`: Frame number or timestamp\n",
        "- `object_id`: Unique identifier per object\n",
        "- `object_type`: Class label (e.g., 'aircraft', 'baggage_cart', 'person')\n",
        "- `x_min, y_min, x_max, y_max`: Bounding box coordinates\n",
        "\n",
        "## 📐 Pipeline Flow\n",
        "\n",
        "```mermaid\n",
        "flowchart TD\n",
        "    A[Load Annotation CSVs] --> B[QA Sanity Checks]\n",
        "    B --> C[Bounding Box Visual Overlay]\n",
        "    C --> D[Convert to COCO Format]\n",
        "    D --> E[Schema Re-validation]\n",
        "    E --> F[Export QA-Ready Dataset]\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "## 🔬 Literature & Standards\n",
        "\n",
        "- Wang et al. (2022). *Airport Apron Monitoring Using Deep Learning on Synthetic Imagery*. [DOI:10.3390/s22082983](https://doi.org/10.3390/s22082983)\n",
        "- Chen et al. (2023). *Foreign Object Detection for Airport Runways Using YOLO*. [IEEE Access](https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/10067897)\n",
        "- Raza et al. (2021). *Visual QA for Surveillance in Critical Infrastructure*. [arXiv:2105.11100](https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.11100)\n",
        "\n",
        "## ✅ Outcome\n",
        "\n",
        "At the end of this notebook, we will have:\n",
        "- Validated bounding box annotations\n",
        "- Visual verification of object labeling\n",
        "- Exported a clean, COCO-compatible dataset\n",
        "\n",
        "This workflow provides a reliable, repeatable QA process that can be adapted to other CV use cases in airside, industrial, or transportation domains.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# 🧪 ML QA & Monitoring for Real-Time Computer Vision\n",
        "This notebook simulates quality assurance logic for real-time CV pipelines, focusing on monitoring inference confidence, detecting model drift, applying anomaly detection techniques, and tracking experiments using MLflow."
      ],
      "id": "8e0f00e1"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "from sklearn.ensemble import IsolationForest"
      ],
      "id": "f3bbab82",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 📥 Load Inference Data"
      ],
      "id": "40f83453"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "data = pd.read_csv('../../_data/CV/synthetic_cv_data.csv')\n",
        "data['timestamp'] = pd.to_datetime(data['timestamp'])\n",
        "data.head()"
      ],
      "id": "19b3d3a7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 📉 Confidence Score Monitoring\n",
        "Visualize the rolling confidence mean to detect potential drift."
      ],
      "id": "a5c31ffe"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "rolling_avg = data['confidence'].rolling(50).mean()\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 5))\n",
        "plt.plot(data['timestamp'], data['confidence'], alpha=0.3, label='Confidence')\n",
        "plt.plot(data['timestamp'], rolling_avg, color='red', label='Rolling Mean (50)')\n",
        "plt.axhline(0.6, linestyle='--', color='gray', label='Alert Threshold')\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "plt.title('Confidence Score Over Time')\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Timestamp')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Confidence')\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "2b740618",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 🚨 Alert Trigger"
      ],
      "id": "74aa34c9"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "if rolling_avg.iloc[-1] < 0.6:\n",
        "    print(\"⚠️ ALERT: Confidence degradation detected!\")\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(\"✅ System performance is stable.\")"
      ],
      "id": "6cea5814",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 🤖 Anomaly Detection via Isolation Forest"
      ],
      "id": "140b2c84"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "features = data[['bbox_area', 'confidence']]\n",
        "model = IsolationForest(contamination=0.05, random_state=42)\n",
        "data['anomaly'] = model.fit_predict(features)\n",
        "data['anomaly'] = data['anomaly'].map({1: 'Normal', -1: 'Anomaly'})\n",
        "data['anomaly'].value_counts()"
      ],
      "id": "397d8131",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 🔍 Visualize Anomalies"
      ],
      "id": "b229266d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 5))\n",
        "colors = {'Normal': 'blue', 'Anomaly': 'red'}\n",
        "for label, group in data.groupby('anomaly'):\n",
        "    plt.scatter(group['timestamp'], group['confidence'], c=colors[label], label=label, alpha=0.6)\n",
        "plt.title('Detected Anomalies in Confidence')\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Timestamp')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Confidence')\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "456cce46",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 📦 MLflow Logging\n",
        "Log model parameters, performance metrics, and version metadata using MLflow."
      ],
      "id": "016674f9"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import mlflow\n",
        "import mlflow.sklearn\n",
        "\n",
        "# Start an MLflow run\n",
        "with mlflow.start_run(run_name=\"cv_qa_drift_monitoring\"):\n",
        "    mlflow.log_param(\"model_type\", \"IsolationForest\")\n",
        "    mlflow.log_param(\"contamination\", 0.05)\n",
        "    mlflow.log_metric(\"anomaly_count\", (data['anomaly'] == \"Anomaly\").sum())\n",
        "    mlflow.log_metric(\"mean_confidence\", data['confidence'].mean())\n",
        "    mlflow.log_metric(\"rolling_avg_last\", rolling_avg.iloc[-1])\n",
        "    mlflow.sklearn.log_model(model, \"model\")\n",
        "    mlflow.set_tag(\"version\", \"v1.0\")\n",
        "    mlflow.set_tag(\"context\", \"QA pipeline drift detection\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"✅ MLflow run logged.\")"
      ],
      "id": "a22a8d67",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 🧩 Simulated `kubectl` Logs for ML System Monitoring\n",
        "Real-time ML pipelines are often deployed in Kubernetes pods. QA engineers frequently inspect pod logs and system status using `kubectl`. Below is a simulated log parser that mimics reading pod health and anomaly alerts from a log file."
      ],
      "id": "66d51c9a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import time\n",
        "\n",
        "# Simulated kubectl logs (mocked string output)\n",
        "kubectl_logs = \"\"\"\n",
        "[2025-06-20 08:01:13] pod/vision-inferencer Ready\n",
        "[2025-06-20 08:01:19] INFO: Inference pipeline started.\n",
        "[2025-06-20 08:01:22] WARN: Confidence dropped below 0.65\n",
        "[2025-06-20 08:01:25] ALERT: Detected anomaly cluster in frame stream 41\n",
        "[2025-06-20 08:01:30] pod/vision-inferencer Healthy\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display line-by-line to mimic real-time stream\n",
        "for line in kubectl_logs.strip().split('\\n'):\n",
        "    print(line)\n",
        "    time.sleep(0.3)"
      ],
      "id": "a54fc992",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## ✅ Next Steps\n",
        "- Monitor system metrics via Prometheus/Grafana\n",
        "- Deploy QA checks in CI/CD with pytest\n",
        "- Integrate tracking with MLflow and experiment registry\n",
        "- Simulate larger datasets with DVC for long-term monitoring"
      ],
      "id": "36da0afd"
    }
  ],
